{{- /*
A duration bound, spelled as the declaration spelled it.

The count and the unit rather than the nanoseconds they multiply out to.
Both compile to the same value, and only one of them can be checked
against the stamp a reader is holding: `timeout=100ms` and
`Timeout: 100000000` agree, and nobody can see that they do.

The unit is a symbol, so the import registers through the backend the way
every other reference does — the earlier spelling avoided the import by
emitting the arithmetic already done, which is a saving of one import
line against a number no reader can verify.
*/ -}}
{{- define "model.lawfield.ConstDur" -}}
{{ .Name }}: {{ .Lit }} * {{ renderExpr .Const }}
{{- end -}}
